WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.913
In this lesson we add a conditional column.

2
00:00:03.913 --> 00:00:07.327
On the Add Column tab, choose Conditional Column.

3
00:00:07.327 --> 00:00:09.887
It works like an IF statement:

4
00:00:09.887 --> 00:00:14.580
if a condition is true, return one value, otherwise return another.

5
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:20.317
I name the new column Planning.

6
00:00:20.317 --> 00:00:21.475
The rule is:

7
00:00:21.475 --> 00:00:26.880
if Units Sold is less than or equal to one thousand, then output zero.

8
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:37.131
In the Else box I type:

9
00:00:37.131 --> 00:00:39.618
We will sell this product next year.

10
00:00:39.618 --> 00:00:43.880
So products that sold more than one thousand units get this message.

11
00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:06.223
Click OK, and the Planning column appears at the end of the table.

12
00:01:06.223 --> 00:01:11.420
I move it next to Units Sold, so we can check the rule row by row.

13
00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:40.652
Rows with one thousand units or fewer show zero, and the rest show our message.

14
00:01:40.652 --> 00:01:46.680
A number and text in the same column is not ideal, so let's improve the output.

15
00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:57.164
I open the step again with the gear icon in Applied Steps, and change

16
00:01:57.164 --> 00:01:59.378
the zero to a clear label:

17
00:01:59.378 --> 00:02:00.116
STOP SELLING.

18
00:02:00.116 --> 00:02:01.960
Now both results are text.

19
00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:22.227
Be careful when you delete steps.

20
00:02:22.227 --> 00:02:27.424
Here a later step still refers to Planning, so once that column is gone,

21
00:02:27.424 --> 00:02:29.279
Power Query shows an error:

22
00:02:29.279 --> 00:02:32.620
the column Planning of the table was not found.

23
00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:47.760
The fix is to delete or edit the step that depends on the missing column.

